(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["central-ideas-and-details_2"] = [{"id":"dcca0dfc","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The following text is from Mick Herron’s 2023 novel The Secret Hours. The narrator is describing members of a government committee. Finally, and adding much-needed gravitas, was Sir Winston Day, whose features seemed moulded to adorn a bust, or possibly a stamp, and whose forehead was so evidently bulging with grey matter that it would have been impertinent to inquire too closely into the actual achievements his half century of public service had produced. His recently published memoirs possibly cast light on this enigma, but given that such details were not provided until after the thirty-page mark, they might as well have remained state secrets. ©2023 by Mick Herron Based on the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Mick Herron’s 2023 novel The Secret Hours. The narrator is describing members of a government committee.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Finally, and adding much-needed gravitas, was Sir Winston Day, whose features seemed moulded to adorn a bust, or possibly a","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"stamp, and whose forehead was so evidently bulging with grey matter that it would have been impertinent to inquire too closely","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"into the actual achievements his half century of public service had produced. His recently published memoirs possibly cast light","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"on this enigma, but given that such details were not provided until after the thirty-page mark, they might as well have remained","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"state secrets.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©2023 by Mick Herron","indent":4}],"question":"Based on the text, which choice best describes Sir Winston Day?","choices":["He has the appearance of a distinguished figure, but it is uncertain whether he has accomplished anything to earn distinction.","He looks like a person worthy of respect, but his memoirs reveal that some of his actions were dishonorable.","He would be a celebrated public figure if his achievements did not have to be kept secret.","He has maintained a modest profile even though he has served the public capably for many years."]},{"id":"0d81b7d9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Paleontologist Alan Tennyson and colleagues studied fossil bones found in New Zealand that are more than 55 million years old. The researchers determined that the fossil bones belonged to two previously unknown species of prehistoric penguins. Moreover, they estimated that one of the two penguin species was more than three times the size of the emperor penguin, which is the largest penguin species that exists today. Based on the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Paleontologist Alan Tennyson and colleagues studied fossil bones found in New Zealand that are more than 55 million years old. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"researchers determined that the fossil bones belonged to two previously unknown species of prehistoric penguins. Moreover, they estimated that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"one of the two penguin species was more than three times the size of the emperor penguin, which is the largest penguin species that exists","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"today.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the text, which choice best describes the two previously unknown penguin species?","choices":["They are frequently studied by paleontologists.","They are no longer living species.","They were smaller than penguin species that exist today.","They spent little of their lives in water."]},{"id":"ad680167","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The recovery of a 1,000-year-old Chinese shipwreck in the Java Sea near present-day Indonesia has yielded a treasure trove of artifacts, including thousands of small ceramic bowls. Using a portable X-ray fluorescence analyzer tool, Lisa Niziolek and her team were able to detect the chemical composition of these bowls without damaging them. By comparing the chemical signatures of the bowls with those of the materials still at old Chinese kiln sites, Niziolek and her team can pinpoint which Chinese kilns likely produced the ceramic bowls.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The recovery of a 1,000-year-old Chinese shipwreck in the Java Sea near present-day Indonesia has yielded a treasure trove of artifacts, including","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"thousands of small ceramic bowls. Using a portable X-ray fluorescence analyzer tool, Lisa Niziolek and her team were able to detect the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"chemical composition of these bowls without damaging them. By comparing the chemical signatures of the bowls with those of the materials","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"still at old Chinese kiln sites, Niziolek and her team can pinpoint which Chinese kilns likely produced the ceramic bowls.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Because of a new technology, researchers can locate and recover more shipwrecks than they could in the past.","Researchers have been able to identify the location of a number of Chinese kilns in operation 1,000 years ago.","With the help of a special tool, researchers have determined the likely origin of bowls recovered from a shipwreck.","Before the invention of portable X-ray fluorescence, researchers needed to take a small piece out of an artifact to analyze its components."]},{"id":"64b6427a","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Since its completion in 2014, Bosco Verticale (Vertical Forest) — a pair of residential towers in Milan, Italy, covered by vegetation —has become a striking symbol of environmental sustainability in architecture. Stefano Boeri intended his design, which features balconies that are home to hundreds of trees, to serve as a model for promoting urban biodiversity. However, the concept has faced skepticism: critics note that although the trees used in Bosco Verticale were specifically cultivated for the project, it’s too early to tell if they can thrive in this unusual setting.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Since its completion in 2014, Bosco Verticale (Vertical Forest)—a pair of residential towers in Milan, Italy, covered by vegetation—has become a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"striking symbol of environmental sustainability in architecture. Stefano Boeri intended his design, which features balconies that are home to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"hundreds of trees, to serve as a model for promoting urban biodiversity. However, the concept has faced skepticism: critics note that although","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the trees used in Bosco Verticale were specifically cultivated for the project, it’s too early to tell if they can thrive in this unusual setting.","indent":0}],"question":"According to the text, why are some critics skeptical of the concept behind Bosco Verticale?","choices":["Some essential aspects of Bosco Verticale’s design are difficult to adapt to locations other than Milan.","The plant life on Bosco Verticale ended up being less varied than Boeri had envisioned it would be.","The construction of Bosco Verticale was no less environmentally damaging than the construction of more conventional buildings is.","It is unclear whether Bosco Verticale can support the plant life included in its design."]},{"id":"b62cb782","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Culinary anthropologist Vertamae Smart-Grosvenor may be known for her decades of work in national public television and radio, but her book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is likely her most influential project. The 1970 book, whose title refers to Smart- Grosvenor’s roots in the Low Country of South Carolina, was unusual for its time. It combined memoir, recipes, travel writing, and social commentary and challenged notions about conventions of food and cooking. Long admired by many, the book and its author have shaped contemporary approaches to writing about cuisine.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Culinary anthropologist Vertamae Smart-Grosvenor may be known for her decades of work in national public television and radio, but her book","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is likely her most influential project. The 1970 book, whose title refers to Smart-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Grosvenor’s roots in the Low Country of South Carolina, was unusual for its time. It combined memoir, recipes, travel writing, and social","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"commentary and challenged notions about conventions of food and cooking. Long admired by many, the book and its author have shaped","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"contemporary approaches to writing about cuisine.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the main idea of the text?","choices":["Smart-Grosvenor’s unconventional book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl is an important contribution to food writing.","Smart-Grosvenor held many different positions over her life, including reporter and food writer.","Smart-Grosvenor’s groundbreaking book Vibration Cooking: or, the Travel Notes of a Geechee Girl didn’t receive the praise it deserved when it was first published in 1970.","Smart-Grosvenor was a talented chef whose work inspired many people to start cooking for themselves."]},{"id":"dc5edbf6","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Microplastics are pieces of plastic that are smaller than a grain of rice. These small plastics can be found in large quantities in ocean waters. Ecologist Jessica Reichert and her team are studying the role reef-building corals have in capturing microplastics from ocean waters. Through research, her team has found that these corals may be storing up to 20 million kilograms of microplastics each year in their skeletons and tissues.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Microplastics are pieces of plastic that are smaller than a grain of rice. These small plastics can be found in large quantities in ocean waters.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Ecologist Jessica Reichert and her team are studying the role reef-building corals have in capturing microplastics from ocean waters. Through","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"research, her team has found that these corals may be storing up to 20 million kilograms of microplastics each year in their skeletons and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"tissues.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["Ecologists are interested in learning more about how certain corals build large reefs.","Questions remain around the impact certain corals have on ocean ecosystems.","Microplastics are small pieces of plastic that can be found in ocean waters.","Ecologists predict that corals store large amounts of microplastics from ocean waters."]},{"id":"04bcb7a9","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Xin Wang and colleagues have discovered the earliest known example of a flower bud in a 164-million-year-old plant fossil in China. The researchers have named the new species Florigerminis jurassica. They believe that the discovery pushes the emergence of flowering plants, or angiosperms, back to the Jurassic period, which occurred between 145 million and 201 million years ago.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Xin Wang and colleagues have discovered the earliest known example of a flower bud in a 164-million-year-old plant fossil in China. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"researchers have named the new species Florigerminis jurassica. They believe that the discovery pushes the emergence of flowering plants, or","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"angiosperms, back to the Jurassic period, which occurred between 145 million and 201 million years ago.","indent":0}],"question":"According to the text, how old was the fossil that Wang and colleagues discovered?","choices":["150 million years old","145 million years old","164 million years old","201 million years old"]},{"id":"73caa3ab","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The following text is from Mark Haber’s 2022 novel Saint Sebastian’s Abyss. The narrator and Schmidt are both art critics. When my first wife admitted to Schmidt over dinner that she didn’t find art, painting in particular, especially compelling, Schmidt winced, set down his fork, and sighed dramatically; he then excused himself, explaining an appointment he d forgotten about had suddenly and inexplicably been remembered, while making it abundantly clear there was no appointment at all. ©2022 by Mark Haber Based on the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Mark Haber’s 2022 novel Saint Sebastian’s Abyss. The narrator and Schmidt are both art critics.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"When my first wife admitted to Schmidt over dinner that she didn’t find art, painting in particular, especially compelling, Schmidt","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"winced, set down his fork, and sighed dramatically; he then excused himself, explaining an appointment he’d forgotten about had","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"suddenly and inexplicably been remembered, while making it abundantly clear there was no appointment at all.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"©2022 by Mark Haber","indent":4}],"question":"According to the text, what is notable about Schmidt’s behavior?","choices":["Schmidt is only given to theatrical behavior when in the company of the narrator and his first wife.","Schmidt’s absentmindedness regarding his schedule is uncharacteristic of him.","Schmidt’s departure is occasioned by the resumption of a previous disagreement with the narrator’s first wife about a particular painting.","Schmidt conveys his feelings about one of his dining companions without explicitly stating them."]},{"id":"4d3e3c52","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"In a paper about p-i-n planar perovskite solar cells (one of several perovskite cell architectures designed to collect and store solar power), Lyndsey McMillon-Brown et al. describe a method for fabricating the cell’s electronic transport layer (ETL) using a spray coating. Conventional ETL fabrication is accomplished using a solution of nanoparticles. The process can result in a loss of up to 80% of the solution, increasing the cost of manufacturing at scale —an issue that may be obviated by spray coating fabrication, which the researchers describe as “highly reproducible, concise, and practical.”","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In a paper about p-i-n planar perovskite solar cells (one of several perovskite cell architectures designed to collect and store solar power),","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Lyndsey McMillon-Brown et al. describe a method for fabricating the cell’s electronic transport layer (ETL) using a spray coating. Conventional","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ETL fabrication is accomplished using a solution of nanoparticles. The process can result in a loss of up to 80% of the solution, increasing the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cost of manufacturing at scale—an issue that may be obviated by spray coating fabrication, which the researchers describe as “highly","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"reproducible, concise, and practical.”","indent":0}],"question":"What does the text most strongly suggest about conventional ETL fabrication?","choices":["It is less suitable for manufacturing large volumes of planar p-i-n perovskite solar cells than an alternative fabrication method may be.","It is more expensive when manufacturing at scale than are processes for fabricating ETLs used in other perovskite solar cell architectures.","It typically entails a greater loss of nanoparticle solution than do other established approaches for ETL fabrication.","It is somewhat imprecise and therefore limits the potential effectiveness of p-i-n planar perovskite solar cells at capturing and storing solar power."]},{"id":"8fb67890","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Archaeologists have discovered a runestone in Norway that may contain the earliest example of written words in Scandinavia. Carbon dating at the discovery site revealed that the stone was likely carved between 1 and 250 CE. Runologist Kristel Zilmer believes the stone will be helpful in learning more about the use of runic alphabets in early Iron Age Scandinavia.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Archaeologists have discovered a runestone in Norway that may contain the earliest example of written words in Scandinavia. Carbon dating at","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the discovery site revealed that the stone was likely carved between 1 and 250 CE. Runologist Kristel Zilmer believes the stone will be helpful in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"learning more about the use of runic alphabets in early Iron Age Scandinavia.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main topic of the text?","choices":["Battles of the Iron Age","A runestone found in Norway","A new method for dating rock samples","The research interests of Kristel Zilmer"]},{"id":"34c2e387","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Jürgen Kocka and other historians of capitalism rarely discuss domestic capitalism in Africa before the period of European colonization, implicitly presenting capitalism as external to and imposed on Africa. Crislayne Alfagali and other Africanist scholars have shown, however, that in parts of Africa, returns-focused investment, the establishment of open markets for wage labor, and other features of capitalism predated colonization. One reason for this discrepancy is that historians of capitalism tend to focus on longitudinal economic data drawn from archival records, which do not exist for much of precolonial Africa.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jürgen Kocka and other historians of capitalism rarely discuss domestic capitalism in Africa before the period of European colonization,","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"implicitly presenting capitalism as external to and imposed on Africa. Crislayne Alfagali and other Africanist scholars have shown, however, that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"in parts of Africa, returns-focused investment, the establishment of open markets for wage labor, and other features of capitalism predated","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"colonization. One reason for this discrepancy is that historians of capitalism tend to focus on longitudinal economic data drawn from archival","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"records, which do not exist for much of precolonial Africa.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement about Alfagali and other Africanist scholars is best supported by information in the text?","choices":["They likely make use of different types of evidence than historians of capitalism typically rely on.","They likely differ from historians of capitalism in the methods they use to derive longitudinal economic data from archival records.","They likely have a different view about which activities should be considered capitalist in nature than historians of capitalism do.","They likely view capitalism as having been more beneficial for Africa than historians of capitalism do."]},{"id":"8f3a200e","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Some astronomers searching for extraterrestrial life have proposed that atmospheric NH 3 (ammonia) can serve as a biosignature gas — an indication that a planet harbors life. Jingcheng Huang, Sara Seager, and colleagues evaluated this possibility, finding that on rocky planets, atmospheric NH 3 likely couldn’t reach detectably high levels in the absence of biological activity. But the team also found that on so-called mini- Neptunes — gas planets smaller than Neptune but with atmospheres similar to Neptune’s ’— atmospheric pressure and temperature can be high enough to produce atmospheric NH 3.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Some astronomers searching for extraterrestrial life have proposed that atmospheric NH3 (ammonia) can serve as a biosignature gas—an","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"indication that a planet harbors life. Jingcheng Huang, Sara Seager, and colleagues evaluated this possibility, finding that on rocky planets,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"atmospheric NH3 likely couldn’t reach detectably high levels in the absence of biological activity. But the team also found that on so-called mini-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Neptunes—gas planets smaller than Neptune but with atmospheres similar to Neptune’s—atmospheric pressure and temperature can be high","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"enough to produce atmospheric NH3.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the text, Huang, Seager, and colleagues would most likely agree with which statement about atmospheric NH ?","choices":["Its presence is more likely to indicate that a planet is a mini-Neptune than that the planet is a rocky planet that could support life.","Its absence from a planet that’s not a mini-Neptune indicates that the planet probably doesn’t have life.","It should be treated as a biosignature gas if detected in the atmosphere of a rocky planet but not if detected in the atmosphere of a mini- Neptune.","It doesn’t reliably reach high enough concentrations in the atmospheres of rocky planets or mini-Neptunes to be treated as a biosignature gas."]},{"id":"409058ee","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"To protect themselves when being attacked, hagfish —jawless marine animals that resemble eels — will release large quantities of slimy, mucus- like threads. Because these threads are unusually strong and elastic, scientist Atsuko Negishi and her colleagues have been trying to recreate them in a lab as an eco-friendly alternative to petroleum-based fibers that are often used in fabrics. The researchers want to reproduce the threads in the lab because farming hagfish for their slime would be expensive and potentially harmful to the hagfish.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"To protect themselves when being attacked, hagfish—jawless marine animals that resemble eels—will release large quantities of slimy, mucus-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"like threads. Because these threads are unusually strong and elastic, scientist Atsuko Negishi and her colleagues have been trying to recreate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"them in a lab as an eco-friendly alternative to petroleum-based fibers that are often used in fabrics. The researchers want to reproduce the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"threads in the lab because farming hagfish for their slime would be expensive and potentially harmful to the hagfish.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the text’s main idea?","choices":["The slimy threads that hagfish release might help researchers create a new kind of fabric.","Hagfish have inspired researchers to develop a new petroleum-based fabric.","Hagfish are not well suited to being raised in captivity.","The ability of hagfish to slime their attackers compensates for their being jawless."]},{"id":"2592e0de","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Bicycles were first mass-produced in the late nineteenth century throughout Europe and North America, allowing individuals remarkable freedom to travel longer distances quickly and comfortably. This freedom, coupled with the affordability of the vehicle, made the bicycle immensely popular. Individuals were able to live farther from their workplaces, easily visit neighboring towns, and participate in new leisure and sport activities. Bicycling quickly became a popular social endeavor, with enthusiasts forming local cycling clubs to enjoy these newfound activities with others.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Bicycles were first mass-produced in the late nineteenth century throughout Europe and North America, allowing individuals remarkable freedom","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to travel longer distances quickly and comfortably. This freedom, coupled with the affordability of the vehicle, made the bicycle immensely","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"popular. Individuals were able to live farther from their workplaces, easily visit neighboring towns, and participate in new leisure and sport","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"activities. Bicycling quickly became a popular social endeavor, with enthusiasts forming local cycling clubs to enjoy these newfound activities","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"with others.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main idea of the text?","choices":["The widespread adoption of the bicycle in the late nineteenth century provided new opportunities for people.","The affordability of the bicycle in the late nineteenth century made it the preferred way to travel.","The popularity of the bicycle in the late nineteenth century gave rise to the first cycling clubs.","The mass production of the bicycle in the late nineteenth century made it safer for people to use."]},{"id":"303537cf","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The following text is adapted from Lewis Carroll’s 1889 satirical novel Sylvie and Bruno. A crowd has gathered outside a room belonging to the Warden, an official who reports to the Lord Chancellor. One man, who was more excited than the rest, flung his hat high into the air, and shouted (as well as I could make out) “Who roar for the Sub- Warden?” Everybody roared, but whether it was for the Sub-Warden, or not, did not clearly appear: some were shouting “Bread!” and some Taxes! , but no one seemed to know what it was they really wanted. All this I saw from the open window of the Warden’s breakfast-saloon, looking across the shoulder of the Lord Chancellor. “","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Lewis Carroll’s 1889 satirical novel Sylvie and Bruno. A crowd has gathered outside a room belonging to the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Warden, an official who reports to the Lord Chancellor.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"One man, who was more excited than the rest, flung his hat high into the air, and shouted (as well as I could make out) “Who roar for the Sub-","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Warden?” Everybody roared, but whether it was for the Sub-Warden, or not, did not clearly appear: some were shouting “Bread!” and some","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"“Taxes!”, but no one seemed to know what it was they really wanted.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"All this I saw from the open window of the Warden’s breakfast-saloon, looking across the shoulder of the Lord Chancellor.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"“What can it all mean?” he kept repeating to himself. “I never heard such shouting before—and at this time of the morning, too! And with such","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"unanimity!”","indent":0}],"question":"What can it all mean?","choices":["He asks about the meaning of the crowd’s shouting, even though he claims to know what the crowd wants.","He indicates a desire to speak to the crowd, even though the crowd has asked to speak to the Sub-Warden.","He expresses sympathy for the crowd’s demands, even though the crowd’s shouting annoys him.","He describes the crowd as being united, even though the crowd clearly appears otherwise."]},{"id":"82d2436a","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"The following text is from Laila Lalami’s 2019 novel The Other Americans. The narrator is a member of her middle school’s jazz band. One day the jazz band was invited to perform at the Summer Festival in Palm Springs. Walking across the stage to the piano, I did what my teacher had advised. Pretend you’re only playing for one person. That way you won’t be so nervous. I glanced at my father, who sat in the front row, leaning his head just so, waiting. Then I closed my eyes, and began to play. ©2019 by Laila Lalami According to the text,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Laila Lalami’s 2019 novel The Other Americans. The narrator is a member of her middle school’s jazz band.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"One day the jazz band was invited to perform at the Summer Festival in Palm Springs. Walking across the stage to the piano, I did","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"what my teacher had advised. Pretend you’re only playing for one person. That way you won’t be so nervous. I glanced at my","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"father, who sat in the front row, leaning his head just so, waiting. Then I closed my eyes, and began to play.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"©2019 by Laila Lalami","indent":4}],"question":"According to the text, what does the narrator do as she walks across the stage?","choices":["She thinks about the differences between playing the piano alone and playing in a band.","She feels excitement about playing in a music festival for the first time.","She remembers how hard she has practiced for the performance.","She follows her teacher’s advice about managing her nervousness."]}];
